# nr-office-pdf-colour: modules color, function, function_ps of crate mixdog-pdf, their twin test and fixture set office-colour. Written; the three modules are not declared yet.

## 1. native/core/crates/mixdog-pdf/src/lib.rs: declare the modules
Add three lines to the `pub mod` list, each in alphabetical place:
    pub mod color;          (after `pub mod codec_glue;`)
    pub mod function;       (after `pub mod fonts;`)
    pub mod function_ps;    (after `pub mod function;`)
Nothing to re-export: callers use `mixdog_pdf::color::{parse, ColorSpace}` and `mixdog_pdf::function::{create, PdfFunction}`.
The doc comment at the head of lib.rs names the modules "declared here so later tasks each own their files"; add `color`, `function`,
`function_ps` to the parenthesised list there if it is kept in step.

## 2. native/core/crates/mixdog-pdf/Cargo.toml
[dependencies], one new workspace edge (V8-exact `Math.pow`, `Math.log`, `Math.min`, `Math.max`, `Math.round` of mixdog_js::math; the
entry `mixdog-js = { path = "crates/mixdog-js" }` exists in [workspace.dependencies]):
    mixdog-js = { workspace = true }
[dev-dependencies], for the twin test (reads the recording and runs the ignored re-record through the test kit; `mixdog-testkit` is a
workspace dependency):
    mixdog-testkit = { workspace = true }
Neither crate is in the hakari set for mixdog-pdf (mixdog-pdf and mixdog-js are both in `final-excludes` of native/core/.config/hakari.toml):
no mixdog-workspace-hack edge.

## 3. native/core/Cargo.lock
Only the package entry of mixdog-pdf changes; its dependency list becomes (alphabetical, dev-dependencies included as Cargo writes them):
