## 5. No SERVICE_PENDING names, no protocol rows, no hot file beyond the three above: the modules register no service.

## 6. Seams for the tasks that use the colour layer (nothing to wire now)
- `color::parse(cs: &Obj, xref: &Xref, resources: Option<&Dict>) -> Result<Arc<ColorSpace>>` is `ColorSpaceUtils.parse`;
  `resources` is the dictionary a colour space name is looked up in (the page's or form's `/Resources`).
- `ColorSpace::{get_rgb, get_rgb_hex, get_rgb_item, get_rgb_items, get_rgb_buffer, fill_rgb, is_default_decode, is_passthrough,
  uses_zero_to_one_range, num_comps, name}` are the methods of pdf.js's `ColorSpace`; `get_rgb_buffer` takes the components of any
  unsigned or float element type that converts to f64. `fill_rgb` carries the three resizers it calls, so the image task
  only decodes and calls it.
- `function::create(xref, obj, parse_array) -> Result<PdfFunction>` is `PDFFunctionFactory.create`; `PdfFunction::call(src, dest)`.
  The operator-list task (setFillColor and shading functions) uses both.
- pdf.js caches parsed colour spaces and functions by reference and name; the cache is the caller's to add (it changes no result).

## 7. Verify (after 1 to 3)
cargo nextest run -p mixdog-pdf --offline
cargo clippy -p mixdog-pdf --all-targets --offline -- -D warnings
The ignored `twin_live_colour` re-records with Node (`node benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-colour.mjs --tree <tree>`).
